Remote-tracking refs (`refs/remotes/**` outside `ralph/`) that move, appear or are deleted during a run are now a `repo.integrity_warning` event on the run and card timeline, not a run failure — decision recorded in spec 19 and the docs.

- `src/server/integrity.ts`: new exported `inspectRepoIntegrity()` returning `{ violations, warnings }`; non-managed `refs/remotes/**` diffs (same `ref moved` / `ref appeared` / `ref deleted` wording) land in `warnings`, so they never trigger the lease re-read. `checkRepoIntegrity` is a thin wrapper over `.violations` — signature and `Promise<string[]>` return unchanged, so `reviewService.ts`'s pre-merge `checkRefs: false` call is untouched; `refWritesSince` / `waitForRepoLeaseRelease` (spec 25 decision 6) and `isManagedRef` (`refs/heads/ralph/`, `refs/remotes/<remote>/ralph/` — still skipped entirely, neither violation nor warning) are unchanged.
- `src/server/stage.ts`: `integrityViolationReason` takes `{ cardId, runId }`, emits `repo.integrity_warning` (payload `{ refs: [...] }`) whether or not the run also has real violations, and fails only on violations; callers in `orchestrator.ts` / `evaluationService.ts` pass the ids.
- `src/app/card/[id]/page.tsx`: renders the event as an amber "⚠ Remote-tracking refs changed during the run" card listing `payload.refs`, falling back to the raw event row when the payload is not shaped that way.
- Why: a `git fetch origin` / `git push` in the registered checkout `/repos/radulf` (2026-09-24) moved `refs/remotes/origin/beta` and created `refs/remotes/origin/feat/retry-context` and failed a run whose commits were intact. Nothing in Radulf reads remote-tracking refs to decide what lands — spec 29's base sync merges the local base branch, delivery pushes `ralph/*`, merges target local branches.
